  "memory_contract": "Writable four/eight-byte range and no pointer wrap. All finite prefixes have actual partial byte-store content, preserve all permissions and memory outside the written prefix. Full returns have exact little-endian bytes. Loss retains current memory; actual first-byte-loss witness and fresh unaligned ownership witnesses are checked.",
