      "max_steps_including_loss": 75
    }
  },
  "roundtrip": "For all 32/64-bit words, bitwise codec identities and actual source writer-to-reader memory connections recover the original word; every completed reader return is exact. This does not certify a frame caller or provide a C-to-Lean proof translation.",
  "foundation_review": "Three local memory identities adapt the LGPL upstream Memory.v proofs and derive proof irrelevance from already-audited Classical_Prop.classic; Axioms.proof_irr is not added. Attribution and LGPL terms are retained in WriteBytes.v and connection/LICENSES.md.",
